  "findings": [
    "All four authored 2x2 material tiles were inspected against the matched baseline tiles. No hard linear wrap boundary was visible in these views; periodic repetition still exists.",
    "Final r8b bark retains longitudinal fissures and cortex shoulders in close, mid-distance, opposed grazing and dim-grazing views. The final AO calibration did not regress the accepted shape. Its surface detail remains simpler and less photographically rich than the historical scanned bark.",
    "Weathered structural timber and counter timber remain distinct in color and roughness. The unchanged world cameras and lighting preserve the intended warm wooden street character.",
    "Low-contrast moss/mineral rock preserves the subdued distant landscape character better than the earlier gray-only study. It is a shared-role compromise, not a measured scan.",
    "Both sides of the three world comparisons use identical disclosed denoising; raw renders are retained. Material studio, tiles, trunk and rock proofs remain undenoised."
  ],
  "limitations": [
    "Art admission applies only to the exact map/plan/preview hashes recorded here. It is not proof that the Unity installer has executed.",
    "No scan-equivalent photorealism, Unity shader equivalence, BC-compression quality, mip behavior, parallax calibration or headset comfort is asserted.",
    "Primitive endcaps are not authored endgrain; height relief does not change mesh silhouettes. Existing secondary UV scales retain their original variation.",
    "Unity/Udon compilation, import, repeat installation, save/reload, network, audio, bake, Build & Test, VRChat upload and actual performance remain untested."
  ]
